{
  "name": "NADH regeneration by formate dehydrogenase (reference case)",
  "version": "2",
  "description": "Reaction model of the oxidation of formate to carbon dioxide by NAD+-dependent formate dehydrogenase (FDH, EC 1.17.1.9), used to regenerate NADH. The rate law is the initial-rate form of an ordered bi-bi mechanism in which NAD+ binds first. Formate is represented by formic acid, so that the reaction is balanced in atoms. The kinetic parameters are representative, rounded values of the order of magnitude reported for the enzyme of Candida boidinii near 30 degC and pH 7.5; they illustrate the workflow and are not a curated measurement.",
